# Third-party licenses

Sustain (`sustain`) is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later. Its release binaries
statically link the Rust crates listed below, so each crate's license and
required copyright notices are reproduced here in full, as their terms
oblige.

**This file is generated — do not edit it by hand.** It is produced from the
locked dependency graph (`Cargo.lock`) by [`cargo about`], which reads each
crate's actual `LICENSE`/`NOTICE` files rather than trusting its SPDX
metadata string. CI regenerates it and fails on any drift, so a dependency
change that alters the attribution set surfaces as a diff in the same change.
Regenerate with:

```sh
cargo about generate --frozen --fail about.hbs -o THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md
```

The dynamically linked platform stack — GTK 4, GStreamer, GLib, Cairo, Pango,
and the rest of GNOME — is **not** redistributed by Sustain: the Debian
package depends on the distribution's own packages for it, and the Flatpak
draws it from the `org.gnome.Platform` runtime. Those components ship their
own notices, so they are intentionally absent here.

This file is installed at `/usr/share/doc/sustain/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md` in
the Debian package and at
`/app/share/licenses/io.github.open_sustain.sustain/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md`
in the Flatpak.

[`cargo about`]: https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about

